VeridianOS: kdesu: read --attach/--embed only when they are defined (X11)

GCC reported -Wunused-but-set-variable for 'winid' in main()
(kdesu/kdesu.cpp): with WITH_X11 off, the only use of winid (attaching the
password dialog with KWindowSystem::setMainWindow()) is compiled out.

The --attach and --embed options are themselves registered only under
WITH_X11, yet main() always queried them. QCommandLineParser::isSet() on
an option that was never added prints "QCommandLineParser: option not
defined" for each, so every kdesu run in a build without X11 logged two
spurious warnings. The winid/attach parsing is now under WITH_X11 like the
option definitions and the code that uses the result. X11 builds are
unchanged.

--- a/kdesu/kdesu.cpp	2026-10-08 17:28:19.357747419 -0400
+++ b/kdesu/kdesu.cpp	2026-10-08 17:28:38.764601701 -0400
@@ -283,6 +283,8 @@
     bool keep = !p.isSet(QStringLiteral("n")) && have_daemon;
     bool terminal = p.isSet(QStringLiteral("t"));
     bool withIgnoreButton = !p.isSet(QStringLiteral("noignorebutton"));
+#if WITH_X11
+    // --attach and --embed are only defined, and the winid only used, with X11
     int winid = -1;
     bool attach = p.isSet(QStringLiteral("attach"));
     if (attach) {
@@ -301,6 +303,7 @@
             qCWarning(category) << "Specified winid to attach to is not a valid number";
         }
     }
+#endif
 
     QList<QByteArray> env;
     QByteArray options;
